{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-3475","published":"2026-08-20T10:00:54Z","modified":"2026-08-20T10:15:14.174949455Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-17543","CVE-2026-7260"],"summary":"php security update","details":"PHP is an HTML-embedded scripting language. PHP attempts to make it easy for developers to write dynamically generated web pages. PHP also offers built-in database integration for several commercial and non-commercial database management systems, so writing a database-enabled webpage with PHP is fairly simple. The most common use of PHP coding is probably as a replacement for CGI scripts. The php package contains the module (often referred to as mod_php) which adds support for the PHP language to Apache HTTP Server.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nImproper escaping of backslashes in attacker-provided parameters would allow for trivial SQL injection in PHP versions from 8.2.* before 8.2.33, from 8.3.* before 8.3.33, from 8.4.* before 8.4.24, and from 8.5.* before 8.5.9.(CVE-2026-17543)\n\nCircular symbolic links in phar archives could lead to unbounded recursion, exhausting the C stack and crashing the PHP process, in PHP versions from 8.2.* before 8.2.33, from 8.3.* before 8.3.33, from 8.4.* before 8.4.24, and from 8.5.* before 8.5.9.(CVE-2026-7260)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"php","ecosystem":"openEuler:20.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/php&distro=openEuler-20.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.0.30-16.oe2003sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["php-8.0.30-16.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-bcmath-8.0.30-16.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-cli-8.0.30-16.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-common-8.0.30-16.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-dba-8.0.30-16.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-dbg-8.0.30-16.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-debuginfo-8.0.30-16.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-debugsource-8.0.30-16.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-devel-8.0.30-16.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-embedded-8.0.30-16.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-enchant-